# Named `Dockerfile.dockerignore`, not `.dockerignore`, and lives here in api/deploy/ rather than
# the api/ context root — Docker's own convention: for a build invoked with `-f
# api/deploy/Dockerfile` and `context: api` (see api/deploy/docker-compose*.yml and the CI
# workflow), it looks for `<dockerfile-path-relative-to-context>.dockerignore` in the context root
# before falling back to a plain `.dockerignore` there. Since `deploy/Dockerfile.dockerignore` is
# itself a valid path within the api/ context, this resolves to this exact file (same convention
# this repo already verified empirically before the api/ consolidation — see CLAUDE.md) — a
# Dockerfile-specific ignore file physically alongside the Dockerfile it governs.
#
# Every pattern below is relative to api/ (the context root) now, not the repo root — webui/ isn't
# part of this context at all anymore, so there's no webui/node_modules line to exclude.
#
# Dockerignore matching is NOT gitignore-style — a bare pattern like `.venv` only matches at the
# context root, not at any depth (unlike git's own .gitignore). `**/` is required to match these
# wherever they actually occur (.venv, **/__pycache__, etc).
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
static/workspace
tests
mcp_server/tests
ingestion_worker/tests
